exercicios.explicacao_md:
The Python track taught you to build the engine. Here you build the dashboard people actually touch — and a broken dashboard is the only part the customer ever sees.

In the browser, **JavaScript** brings the page to life. You select an element with `document.getElementById("id")` and react to clicks with `.addEventListener("click", handler)`.

```js
button.addEventListener("click", function () {
  counter = counter + 1;
});
```

The preview on the right updates by itself — click and see.

