exercicios.explicacao_md:
Rendering data means turning a list into a screen. The pattern is: walk the array, build a piece of HTML for each item and **join it all together** before writing to the DOM.

```js
var html = "";
products.forEach(function (p) {
  html += "<li>" + p.name + "</li>";
});
list.innerHTML = html;   // write ONCE, at the end
```

The classic mistake is using `=` inside the loop (`list.innerHTML = ...`): on every pass you **wipe out** what was already there and only the last item survives. Accumulate with `+=` instead, or build the whole string and write it afterwards. The preview on the right updates by itself.

