exercicios.explicacao_md:
Every HTML tag has a list of CSS **classes**, and JavaScript works with it through `element.classList`:

- `classList.add("x")` — adds the class (if it's already there, nothing changes)
- `classList.remove("x")` — removes the class
- `classList.toggle("x")` — **turns it on if it's off, and off if it's on**
- `classList.contains("x")` — returns `true`/`false`

`toggle` is the ideal shortcut for on/off buttons (light/dark theme, menu open/closed):

```js
button.addEventListener("click", function () {
  document.body.classList.toggle("dark");
});
```

One click applies the theme; the next one undoes it — without any `if`. The preview on the right reflects the change instantly.

